+# output is pure cost. Measured on the target node with 8 ranks inside CUDA
+# graphs, as the full GEMM's time minus the row block's GEMM and all-gather,
+# per call: -3 us at 1024 total rows, +27 us at 2048 and +572 us at 16384,
+# with outputs bitwise equal to the full GEMM at every size. The floor is the
+# smallest measured size that saves time. It counts total rows, so it was
+# set for that 8-rank split. M is the same on every rank and fixed for each
+# captured graph, so every rank takes the same branch.
+UNPOOLER_MIN_TOTAL_ROWS = 2048
+
+# Fewest total rows at which the MoE pooler and its pre-expert norm are split
+# by rows. The pooler's row block does the unpooler's multiply-adds per row and
+# gathers half the bytes per row (M x 4096): measured on the same 8 ranks in
+# graphs, 70 us at 2048 total rows against 122 us for the unpooler's M x 8192
